    "title": "Bayern Munich, Arsenal march on to Champions League semifinals while Real Madrid and Sporting bow out",
    "text": "Luis Díaz's 89th-minute goal broke a 4-4 aggregate deadlock and helped Bayern Munich take out Real Madrid during Wednesday's Champions League quarterfinals.Leading 2-1 heading into the second leg, Bayern Munich were immediately put on the back foot when Arda Güler leveled for Real Madrid in the opening minute after a giveaway by goalkeeper Manuel Neuer.That goal was answered, however, five minutes later by Bayern’s Aleksandar Pavlović, who headed home a corner kick.AdvertisementThe two goals in the opening minutes were a preview for a wild and action-packed first half between the European giants. Güler would score again on a 29th-minute free kick, which was followed by Harry Kane's 50th goal of the season nine minutes later. Just before halftime, Kylian Mbappé leveled it at four on aggregate with his 70th career Champions League goal in only his 98th game.The final 45 minutes didn't have as many goals, but the tension was in the air at the Allianz Arena. It looked as if the match might be headed toward extra time, but Eduardo Camavinga picked up a second yellow card for time wasting to put Real Madrid down to 10 men for the rest of the match.Bayern took advantage and Díaz's curling shot from outside the box minutes later put the hosts up for good. Five minutes after that, Michael Olise made sure Real Madrid was down for the count with a beautiful curling goal.Arsenal returns to the semifinalsArsenal's 0-0 draw with Sporting was enough to move them on to the semifinals 1-0 on aggregate. The draw kept the Gunners' Champions League record this season untarnished (10-0-2) as they get ready to face Atlético Madrid in two weeks.AdvertisementKai Havertz scored the only goal over the two legs in the 91st minute last week in Lisbon.This is the second straight season Arsenal has reached the competition’s semifinals, a first in club history. Last year, the Gunners were beaten 3-1 over two legs by eventual champions PSG.Sporting have now lost their last 11 matches in England and last 11 European knockout matches in a row away from home, which dates back to 1970.Here’s how all of Wednesday’s Champions League action played out live:Live coverage is over23 updatesWed, April 15, 2026 at 4:01 PM CDTSean LeahyAtlético Madrid vs. Arsenal PSG vs. Bayern MunichThe two-legged matches will take place April 28-29 and May 5-6.The 2025-26 Champions League Final will be held on May 30 at Puskás Aréna in Hungary.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 3:59 PM CDTSean LeahyBayern Munich advances 6-4 on aggregate and will meet PSG in the semifinals.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 3:54 PM CDTSean LeahyThe Gunners are in the semifinals and will face Atlético Madrid after knocking out Sporting 1-0 on aggregate.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 3:52 PM CDTSean LeahyMinutes after Eduardo Camavinga was sent off with a second yellow card, Luis Díaz scores just before stoppage time. Bayern Munich leads 5-4 on a aggregate and are minutes from advancing to the semifinal.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 3:49 PM CDTSean LeahyReal Madrid will be down to 10 men for the rest of the match after Eduardo Camavinga committed a foul on Harry Kane and then carried the ball away to waste time. That choice drew a second yellow from referee Slavko Vinčić.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 3:35 PM CDTSean LeahyWed, April 15, 2026 at 3:26 PM CDTSean LeahyWed, April 15, 2026 at 3:04 PM CDTSean LeahyArsenal and Sporting remain deadlocked at 0-0, but the Gunners hold the all-important 1-0 aggregate lead as they look to close out the Portuguese side.Over at Allianz Arena, a five-goal first half sets the stage for a dramatic conclusion to Bayern Munich vs. Real Madrid.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:55 PM CDTSean LeahyWed, April 15, 2026 at 2:46 PM CDTSean LeahyWe have another first-half goal and it’s now 4-4 on aggregate.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:41 PM CDTSean LeahyThe Bayern Munich striker scored the fourth goal of this first half to level the second leg 2-2, but more important give the Bundesliga side the 4-3 edge on aggregate.Kane now has 50 goals in 42 games in all competitions.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:33 PM CDTSean LeahyArda Güler has a second first-half goal as his free kick puts the tie against Bayern Munich back to level at 3-3.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:20 PM CDTSean LeahyWed, April 15, 2026 at 2:19 PM CDTSean LeahyVinícius Júnior is a caution away from being ruled out of the first leg of the semifinal should Real Madrid advance. He was given a stern talking to by referee Slavko Vinčić.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:10 PM CDTSean LeahyWhat an opening six minutes to this match. After Manuel Neuer’s gaffe helped Real Madrid level the tie, Aleksandar Pavlovic heads home a goal off a corner to give Bayern Munich a 3-2 lead on aggregate.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:05 PM CDTSean LeahyA massive error by Bayern goalkeeper Manuel Neuer gifts a goal to Arda Güler. We are now level at two on aggregate after just 40 secondsWed, April 15, 2026 at 2:03 PM CDTSean LeahyThe Bayern Munich goalkeeper would have a chance to break Iker Casillas' record during next season's Champions League campaign.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 2:01 PM CDTSean LeahyBoth matches have kicked off and we are a few hours away from finding out who will join Atlético Madrid and PSG in the Champions League semifinals.Wed, April 15, 2026 at 1:50 PM CDTSean LeahyWed, April 15, 2026 at 1:34 PM CDTSean LeahyThe Liverpool forward went down with a non-contact injury during Tuesday’s loss to Barcelona in the second leg of their Champions League quarterfinal tie.Multiple reports state that the France international will miss at least nine months after he was stretchered off the pitch in the first half. Ekitike is scheduled for scans on Wednesday to determine the severity of the rupture.Champions League quarterfinalsAtlético Madrid advances 3-2 on aggregate over BarcelonaPSG advances 4-0 on aggregate over LiverpoolArsenal advances 1-0 on aggregate over Sporting CPBayern Munich advances 6-4 on aggregate over Real MadridAdvertisementChampions League semifinalsApri